<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">Limb XI &middot; i &mdash; a sub-limb of Consciousness</p>
  <h1>Decoherence &amp; the Remembered Self</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Why the quantum world stops looking quantum; what is genuinely happening inside the
  microtubule, measured rather than cheered; the tide of fluid that washes the brain's scaffolding every night
  and carries away the protein that falls off it; and what physics does and does not permit when a tradition
  says that nothing is lost, and that the whole of a life is picked back up and remembered further along the
  octave.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p>This is the page where three subjects that are usually kept apart are put on one table: a theorem of
    quantum mechanics, a plumbing diagram of the brain, and a claim about what happens to a person. They are
    kept apart for good reasons, and we are going to say exactly where the joins are welded and where they are
    only held together by our hands.</p>
    <p>Our method does not change for the tender subject. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> established and
    checkable &middot; <span class="hist">&#9670;</span> historically documented &middot;
    <span class="spec">&#9670;</span> our own reasoning, offered as reasoning &middot;
    <span class="myth">&#9670;</span> tradition or received teaching, reported as such. If you are here because
    somebody has died, read Part VI first, and know that we will neither sell you a certainty nor take one from
    you.</p>
  </div>
</section>

