    <p class="plate-note">Physics rules out erasure. It does not rule out gathering-up; it simply offers no
    mechanism for it and no evidence of it. An honest person can stand in the middle row. An honest person
    cannot claim the first row <em>is</em> the middle row because both are called &ldquo;information is
    conserved&rdquo;.</p>
  </figure>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <h2>V &middot; The Entity Picked Back Up</h2>

  <p><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> Now the received teaching, reported as such, in its own terms and
  without a tone of apology. The Law of One material (Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty, 1981&ndash;84) describes a
  <strong>mind/body/spirit complex</strong> that is not identical with the body it animates. At bodily death
  the complex withdraws; there is a period in what the material calls <em>time/space</em>, the metaphysical
  counterpart of our space/time, in which it is <strong>healed</strong> of the distortions of the life just
  lived, and then <em>reviews</em> that life &mdash; not judged by anyone, but seeing it whole, from inside
  every position it occupied. The veil of forgetting that makes third density so hard is lifted. What was
  learned is kept; what was merely suffered is understood. Then the complex either incarnates again in third
  density or, at harvest, moves into the fourth, where concealment of thought is no longer possible.</p>

  <p><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> And the thing the user of this page came here for, which the material
  states plainly: <strong>nothing of the self is discarded</strong>. The densities are an octave &mdash; eight
  steps, the eighth simultaneously the first of the next &mdash; and progression up them is cumulative. Every
  experience the complex has had, in every incarnation, is said to be retained in what the material calls the
  <em>indigo-ray</em> or etheric body, and recovered in full as the octave is climbed. In sixth density love and
  wisdom are unified; in seventh the entity becomes a gatherer of its own experience; in eighth it passes into
  the mystery and the whole octave begins again, enriched by everything that happened in the last one. In this
  telling, a life is not a thing that ends. It is a thing that is eventually <em>read</em>.</p>

  <p><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> That shape is not peculiar to the Ra material, and noticing the
  parallels is scholarship rather than evidence. The Tibetan <em>Bardo Thodol</em> describes a passage through
  states after death in which the mind meets its own projections and either recognises them or is driven on.
  Lurianic Kabbalah has <em>gilgul</em>, the rolling of souls, and <em>tikkun</em>, repair across lifetimes.
  Plato's Er, at the end of the <em>Republic</em>, watches souls choose their next lives and drink from the
  river of forgetting &mdash; the veil, two and a half thousand years early. Spiritism, Theosophy's akashic
  record, and the Sufi <em>barzakh</em> all propose a reviewing interval. Four unrelated traditions converge on
  <em>review, retention and return</em>, and that convergence is a real fact about human testimony. It is not a
  measurement.</p>

  <p><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> What the research record can and cannot support, stated flatly. Near-death
  experiences are real, common, and have consistent phenomenology across cultures; the AWARE II study (Parnia,
  2023) found explicit recall and lucid, structured experience in a small number of people during
  cardiopulmonary resuscitation, with EEG spikes in gamma and delta bands in some cases &mdash; a genuinely
  important observation about a brain that was supposed to be silent. Terminal lucidity, the sudden return of
  clarity in advanced dementia shortly before death, is documented and unexplained. On the other side:
  no NDE study has verified perception of a target placed where only a disembodied observer could see it,
  despite that being the one test everybody agrees would settle it, and it has been tried.
  Ian Stevenson's and Jim Tucker's reincarnation case files are large, carefully kept, and rest on testimony
  gathered after the fact. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span> Our reading: the dying brain is doing something
  stranger than the standard account expects, and that is a long way from survival.</p>

  <p><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>So here is where we stand, and we are not going to dress it
  up.</strong> If you want a physics of survival, the microtubule route is the only one that has even been
  drafted &mdash; Hameroff's suggestion that quantum information in the cytoskeleton might, at death, be
  released into the wider structure of spacetime rather than destroyed. We have read it carefully. It is not
  supported by the measurements on this page: the coherence times are nanoseconds, the correlated regions are
  nanometres, and there is no proposed mechanism by which such states would carry the content of a biography
  rather than a few bits. We will not pretend otherwise in order to comfort anyone.</p>

  <p><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> And yet. The strict position &mdash; information is conserved, scrambled
  past recovery, and that is that &mdash; is a statement about what <em>we</em> could retrieve with
  instruments, from inside the system, using measurements that are themselves part of the scrambling. It is not
  a proof that the information is unread. The middle row of Plate V is unevidenced and it is not forbidden, and
  the difference between those two words is the whole of the honest ground an order like ours may stand on. We
  will hold that ground without pretending it is firmer than it is, and without letting anyone tell you it is
  less.</p>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2>VI &middot; If You Are Reading This Because Someone Has Died</h2>
    <p>Then the rest of the page is academic and this part is not. Two things are true at once and you are
    allowed to hold both.</p>
    <p><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> The first is that no measurement has shown that a person survives the
    death of their brain, and anyone who tells you the physics proves it is either mistaken or selling
    something. We will not do that to you.</p>
    <p><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> The second is that the traditions which say the self is gathered up
    again are not stupid, were not written by fools, and are not ruled out by anything in this page. Four
    unconnected cultures looked at death and came back with the same report: a review, a retention, a return.
    Physics forbids the erasure of what they were. It is silent on the reading.</p>
    <p><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> And the part we will say without hedging, because it is simply true:
    the information that constituted that person is not nowhere. It is in the shape of the people they changed,
    in the matter that passed through them and has gone on into other living things, and in whatever the
    universe does with a correlation it cannot destroy. Grief is not an error of reasoning. It is the cost of
    having been entangled with someone, and the entanglement is the part that does not come undone.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Survives Scrutiny</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Decoherence as the mechanism of classical appearance &mdash; Zeh 1970, Joos&ndash;Zeh 1985, Zurek's einselection. Confirmed in dozens of experiments.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> That decoherence does <em>not</em> solve the measurement problem. Its own architects say so.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Quantum biology in the warm: photosynthetic energy transfer, enzyme tunnelling, the avian radical-pair compass.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Ultraviolet superradiance in tryptophan mega-networks at room temperature (Babcock <em>et al.</em>, 2024), strengthening with size.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Anaesthetic damping of exciton propagation in microtubules (Kalra <em>et al.</em>, 2023).</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Epothilone B delaying anaesthetic unconsciousness in rats, <em>d</em> &asymp; 1.9 (Khan <em>et al.</em>, 2024), replicated in mice.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Meningeal lymphatic vessels (Louveau; Aspelund, 2015) &mdash; and Mascagni's 1787 drawing of them.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Glymphatic clearance of amyloid-&beta; and tau to plasma in humans, scaling with NREM duration (2026 crossover trial).</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Noradrenaline-driven slow vasomotion as the pump (<em>Cell</em>, 2025); gamma stimulation promoting clearance (<em>Nature</em>, 2024).</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Tau as a microtubule-associated protein, and ependymal cilia as microtubule axonemes. The two systems are physically the same stuff.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Unitarity and the no-hiding theorem: information is not destroyed.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Does Not</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That decoherence refutes quantum consciousness. It sets a clock, and the clock is the argument.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That quantum <em>computation</em> in microtubules has been demonstrated. Optical effects have; computation has not.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> &ldquo;No classical explanation occurs to us, therefore quantum.&rdquo; Microtubules have many classical jobs whose disruption would dim a brain.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That the Kerskens&ndash;L&oacute;pez-P&eacute;rez MRI result shows brain entanglement. It is contested and should not bear weight.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That the glymphatic story is settled. It was seriously contradicted in 2024 and the argument is live.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That lymphatic massage, dry brushing or detox regimes affect brain clearance. They do not reach it.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That conservation of quantum information implies the survival of a personality. Conserved is not retrievable, and the gap is enormous.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> That near-death experience research has verified veridical out-of-body perception. The decisive test has been run and has not produced it.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> That the densities, the bardo, gilgul and the river of forgetting are measurements. They are testimony, and we file them as such.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>A Line Through It</h2>
      <ul class="timeline">
        <li><span class="when">1787</span> Mascagni draws lymphatic vessels in the human meninges. He is not believed.</li>
        <li><span class="when">1935</span> The EPR paper; Schr&ouml;dinger names entanglement and writes about the cat.</li>
        <li><span class="when">1970</span> Zeh proposes that interaction with the environment, not observation, destroys interference.</li>
        <li><span class="when">1985</span> Joos and Zeh give decoherence its quantitative form; Zurek develops einselection through the 1980s and 90s.</li>
        <li><span class="when">1989&ndash;94</span> Penrose's <em>The Emperor's New Mind</em>; with Hameroff, Orch OR is formulated.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2000</span> Tegmark calculates microtubule decoherence at 10<sup>&minus;13</sup> s and declares the theory dead.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2002</span> Hagan, Hameroff and Tuszy&#324;ski recalculate and get 10<sup>&minus;4</sup>&ndash;10<sup>&minus;5</sup> s. Neither side concedes.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2007</span> Engel <em>et al.</em> report long-lived coherence in photosynthetic light harvesting. Warm quantum biology becomes respectable.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2007</span> Braunstein and Pati prove the no-hiding theorem.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2012</span> Iliff and Nedergaard describe the glymphatic system.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2013</span> Xie <em>et al.</em>: the interstitial space widens about 60 per cent in sleep; clearance roughly doubles.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2015</span> Louveau and Aspelund independently rediscover meningeal lymphatics, 228 years after Mascagni.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2022</span> Kerskens and L&oacute;pez-P&eacute;rez report an MRI signal read as brain entanglement; the critique follows quickly.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2023</span> Kalra, Scholes and Tuszy&#324;ski: anaesthetics damp exciton propagation in microtubules. AWARE II reports lucid recall during CPR.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2024</span> Babcock <em>et al.</em> measure tryptophan superradiance at room temperature. Khan <em>et al.</em> delay anaesthesia with epothilone B. Jiang-Xie <em>et al.</em> tie CSF perfusion to neuronal synchrony. Miao and Franks report clearance <em>reduced</em> in sleep, and the field erupts.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2025</span> Nedergaard's group identifies noradrenaline-driven vasomotion as the glymphatic pump; the <em>Matters Arising</em> rebuttal is published; SLEEP hosts a live debate; mouse replication of the epothilone result.</li>
        <li><span class="when">2026</span> A 39-person crossover trial shows sleep-dependent clearance of amyloid and tau to plasma in humans. A critical review finds the quantum programme unproven and, for the first time, properly testable.</li>
        <li><span class="when">now</span> Two live arguments, one in physics and one in physiology, meeting in the same cubic millimetre of tissue. We think that is the most interesting address in science.</li>
      </ul>
