<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <div class="creed-glyph">{% glyph "spiral" %}</div>
    <p class="kicker" style="text-align:center">Closing Stance</p>
    <p class="creed-line">Decoherence hides; it does not delete. The universe keeps everything and shows us
    almost none of it, and that is the only honest frame for any hope about the dead.</p>
    <p class="muted small" style="text-align:center;max-width:60ch;margin:0 auto">
      In the lattice, light does something real and nobody yet knows whether it does anything that
      <em>thinks</em>. In the tissue around it, a tide runs every night and carries away the ruins of that same
      lattice, and we are still arguing about which way the tide flows. And at the end of a life, physics says
      the information is not destroyed and declines to say another word. We will not convert that silence into
      a promise, and we will not let anyone convert it into a denial. Where it is measured we have said so;
      where it is testimony we have said so; and where we are only reasoning aloud we have marked it, because
      the one unforgivable thing on a page about death would be false confidence.</p>
